          "uco-observable:strings": [
            {
              "@id": "urn:uuid:e44242dd-8d60-5acb-a950-5c4c22595167",
              "@type": "uco-observable:ExtractedString",
              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Case: 2:24-cr-00047-DLB-CJS Doc #: 8 Filed: 10/31/24 Page: 1 of 11 - Page\nID#: 13\n\nUNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT\nEASTERN DISTRICT OF KENTUCKY 31\nNORTHERN DIVISION A'l.'COVlNGTON\nCOVINGTON Hnil<:n it Cnrr\nr:f,L[{l{ U.S, jj/.J'Ul!C J' C(.)!Jl{T\n\nCRIMINAL ACTION NO. 24-47-DLB-CJS\n\nUNITED STATES OF AMERICA PLAINTIFF\n\nv. PLEA AGREEMENT\n\nROBERT MAXWELL WERNER DEFENDANT\n* * * * *\n\n1. Pursuant to Federal Rule of Criminal Procedure 11(c), the Defendant will enter\n\na guilty plea to the Information, charging a violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251(c), employing,\n\nusing, persuading, inducing, enticing, and coercing a minor to engage in sexually explicit\n\nconduct outside the United States, its territories or possessions, for the purpose of\n\nproducing a visual depiction of that conduct.\n\n2. The essential elements of Count 1 of the Infonnation, charging a violation of\n\n18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251(c), are:\n\n(a) The Defendant employed, used, persuaded, induced, enticed or coerced\na minor to engage in sexually explicit conduct outside the United States, its\nterritories or possessions, for the purpose of producing any visual depiction of that\nconduct, or attempted to do so; and\n\n(b) The Defendant intended the visual depiction to be transported to the\nUnited States, or its territories or possessions, by any means, including by using any\nmeans or facility of interstate or foreign commerce or mail; or the Defendant\ntransported the visual depiction to the United States, or its territories or possessions,\nby any means, including by using any means or facility of interstate or foreign\ncommerce or mail.\nCase: 2:24-cr-00047-DLB-CJS Doc #: 8 Filed: 10/31/24 Page: 2 of 11 - Page\nID#: 14\nCase: 2:24-cr-00047-DLB-CJS Doc #: 8 Filed: 10/31/24 Page: 3 of 11 - Page\nID#: 15\nCase: 2:24-cr-00047-DLB-CJS Doc #: 8 Filed: 10/31/24 Page: 4 of 11 - Page\nID#: 16\nCase: 2:24-cr-00047-DLB-CJS Doc #: 8 Filed: 10/31/24 Page: 5 of 11 - Page\nID#: 17\nCase: 2:24-cr-00047-DLB-CJS Doc #: 8 Filed: 10/31/24 Page: 6 of 11 - Page\nID#: 18\nCase: 2:24-cr-00047-DLB-CJS Doc #: 8 Filed: 10/31/24 Page: 7 of 11 - Page\nID#: 19\nCase: 2:24-cr-00047-DLB-CJS Doc #: 8 Filed: 10/31/24 Page: 8 of 11 - Page\nID#: 20\nCase: 2:24-cr-00047-DLB-CJS Doc #: 8 Filed: 10/31/24 Page: 9 of 11 - Page\nID#: 21\nCase: 2:24-cr-00047-DLB-CJS Doc #: 8 Filed: 10/31/24 Page: 10 of 11 - Page\nID#: 22\nCase: 2:24-cr-00047-DLB-CJS Doc #: 8 Filed: 10/31/24 Page: 11 of 11 - Page\nID#: 23"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
